    "body": "## Scope\n\nImplement creation-recovery lifecycle on Draft PR #444 HEAD `bc3687ec582c8f23aab0725c772641afb79942bd`. Only the migration, Worker integration and two authorized tests are changed.\n\n- Migration 0006 backfills all 0003 rows to CLOSED and clears ciphertext without changing battles, capabilities, receipts or outbox.\n- New create rows bind AES-GCM recovery to both original capability digests and generations.\n- Successful first participant commit, capability change/revocation/deletion and terminal scheduler expiry close recovery in the same SQL transaction.\n- Closed requests return `410 CREATION_RECOVERY_CLOSED`; tombstones retain only the idempotency digest. There is no expiry or purge policy.\n\n## Local evidence\n\n- Actual isolated Wrangler/workerd/D1 migrations 0001-0006 and private Worker API suite PASS on the local candidate.\n- Gameplay SQL tests 59/59; hosted and remote D1 offline safety tests 22/22 and 5/5.\n- Repository policy validation PASS, policy tests 17/17, Node syntax and `git diff --check` PASS.\n- Broad `tools` Python suite has the same 15 Stage 7.15 harness errors and 1 unrelated UI-token failure on both this tree and the unchanged PR #444 HEAD; this task edits none of those files.\n\nNo hosted D1, deployment, merge, or production data was used. Please review this exact head independently; it remains Draft.",
